# 900-NRL-0023: Executable QSL overlays bound to a complete supported model — done

**Type:** implementation, `NRL` · **Owner:** Codex (`codex/NRL-lab`) · **Priority:** P1 · **Status:** done (2026-10-26) · **Blocked by:** — · **Roadmap:** G; 900 T04 · **Constitution:** MC-5.2, MC-11.1, MC-11.11, MC-12.1, MC-12.2, MC-12.3, MC-12.4

## Problem

The maintainer requested the five autonomous extensions after the first T11 preparation and host T12/T13 results. Existing host evidence does not establish this extension or native execution.

## Plan

Bind QSL layer replacements to an exact supported decoder base and explicit mapping, preserving external provenance and all untouched weights/tokenizer/state. Export and reload a self-contained executable model. Refuse unsupported base architectures.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Verified source/base/layer geometry bindings; original QSL writer fixture; full logits agree with independent reference; standalone package works after removal of base and overlay inputs; corruption and wrong-base refusals.
- [x] Document the supported profile and limitations, run affected checks on the track branch, preserve reports, and submit an updated landing request.

## Related

- [900](../issues/900-neural-representation-lab.md), T04.
- [NRL](../nrl/README.md). Native T11 remains a separate APP dependency.

## Resolution

Added exact supported-base/layer/fingerprint bindings, an executable QSL model overlay, integrity-checked reload and full standalone export with original tokenizer/weights and complete QSL/binding notices. Four actual transformed FFNs saved by the unchanged QSL writer match independent full PyTorch logits/greedy IDs. A standalone reload runs after removing original source/base/overlay directories. Scope is explicit llama2c/Tinyllamas with NRL model-ID fingerprints; external HF/Qwen standalone formats remain unsupported and broader T04 is not universally closed.

The final NRL profile passes on `b44fbc0d`: 95 host tests, four portable builds and all CLI cycles, including `--expanded`; new external oracles reproduce. [Evidence](../nrl/reports/five-extensions-2026-10-26.json). The full repository gate and code landing belong to the integrator; native T11 remains open.
